## TEXT OVERLAY PATTERNS

When social posts require text on images, follow these platform-specific patterns.

### Text Placement by Platform

| Platform | Safe Zone | Placement | Font Style |
|----------|-----------|-----------|------------|
| Instagram Feed | Bottom 20% | Centered or left-aligned | Clean sans-serif, bold |
| Instagram Stories | Top 15% or bottom 20% | Avoid middle (tap zones) | Bold, high contrast |
| Facebook | Top or bottom 25% | Flexible | Readable, medium weight |
| Pinterest | Top third or bottom banner | Full-width OK | High contrast, decorative OK |
| WhatsApp Status | Bottom 20% | Simple, minimal | Clean, large |

### Text Overlay Principles

**Realism with text:**
- Text should feel DESIGNED, not slapped on
- Respect brand typography ({font_family})
- Ensure contrast for readability (WCAG AA minimum)
- Never obscure key product features
- Text should enhance, not compete with product

**Text types and treatments:**

| Type | Treatment | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| **Headline** | Large, bold, brand font | "NEW ARRIVAL" |
| **Price/offer** | Accent color, prominent | "Rs 499" |
| **CTA** | Button-style or underlined | "Shop Now" |
| **Caption** | Smaller, supporting | "Limited edition" |
| **Feature callout** | With arrow/pointer to product | "Honeycomb texture" |

### Text Legibility Checklist

```
[ ] Contrast ratio sufficient (light on dark or dark on light)?
[ ] Text size readable on mobile (min 24pt equivalent)?
[ ] Font weight appropriate (not too thin)?
[ ] Text doesn't obscure product hero feature?
[ ] Brand typography used consistently?
[ ] Text feels integrated, not pasted on?
```

### When NOT to Use Text

- Catalog hero shots (product should speak)
- Gallery/detail images
- When product packaging has text (competing)
- Lifestyle scenes where mood matters more than message

